    {
      "id": "5f5939c",
      "type": "split",
      "settings": {
        "eyebrow": "Our story",
        "title": "Started in a garage, with one very stubborn starter",
        "text": "<p>Maya Okafor-Lind kept a sourdough starter alive through three moves and a winter without heating. In 2019 she borrowed a deck oven, set it up in a friend’s garage and sold forty loaves from a folding table every Saturday.</p><p>Today the starter, called Gus, lives on Larder Lane, and the folding table is still behind the counter.</p>",
        "image": {
          "src": "/images/oven.svg",
          "alt": "A brick deck oven with a wooden peel"
        },
        "caption": "The deck oven, lit at 4 a.m. every day we’re open.",
        "side": "left",
        "background": "cream",
        "anchor": ""
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
